            <ArticleTitle>[Neurosurgical treatment of trigeminal neuralgia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>761-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sweet's method for thermocoagulation of the Gasserian ganglion is a real advance in the operative treatment of trigeminal neuralgia. The advantages of this method are obvious: minimum operation risk, minimum complication rate, short postoperative convalescence, shorter confinement to hospital and finally the possibility of repeating the operation without risk in the event of a relapse.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
